<title>JAPAN: Nissho Iwai to buy seven Boeings for leasing.</title>
<headline>Nissho Iwai to buy seven Boeings for leasing.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nissho Iwai Corp said on Tuesday it has agreed with Boeing Co to purchase seven passenger airliners for leasing.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the Japanese trading house said it would buy five B737-600s and two B737-300s for a total of $243 million.</p>
<p>The company would take delivery of the aircraft between 1998 and 2001, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Nissho Iwai currently leases 17 airplanes.</p>
</text>
